        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3p2xxRXgxORGXaqv88Nc-46" value="DLT&amp;nbsp; equivalence:&lt;div&gt;Signers of &quot;blecks&quot; are FLI with per LFI kay/identity, and &quot;wholesale/settlemnt retail coin (contract input = output -&amp;gt; avoid double spending)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;opacity=50;verticalAlign=top;align=left;" parent="4WZXP__eG7i2tE0GjdjS-21" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-13161" y="-4569" width="1953" height="219" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3p2xxRXgxORGXaqv88Nc-47" value="- Per LFI customer wallet Database ledger equivalence (all LFIs should be aligned on partial views of the database postgres ledger ...)&lt;div&gt;- Metadata in the DLT about the retail TXs should be also aligned&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;WHAT IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH?&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;SOURCE OF TRUTH IMPLICATION:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- resistant to a rogue/compromised/failed participant (LFI)&lt;br&gt;- In a distributed atomic transaction rollback:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; - Two phase commit logic is needed: what non-repudiation of transaction participant action are in place?&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; -&amp;nbsp; Without two phase commit: who has precedence in reconsiliations?&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;How to sync (with ACID properties) final DLT block notarization with Flexcube , otherwise Flexcube and DLT representation may not be consistant, there&#39;s also the problem of repudiation among systems.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Considerations:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- There&#39;s no direct claim to the DLT (notarized by the CB) from the customer wallets&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;opacity=50;verticalAlign=top;align=left;" parent="4WZXP__eG7i2tE0GjdjS-21" vertex="1">
